Lets the core say that a tab switch is between tabs of one of its split views, which Chrome's tab
strip then doesn't time, as it doesn't between the tabs of its own split (//browser_core/hooks.h).
Both pages are on screen already, so the switch shows nothing new. Timed, a switch to a split's
new tab would end at its page's first frame, once it has loaded, and Chrome would call it a
switch to a tab with a saved frame, since the split showed its view first.

